-- The rules of `Reject.Default.yana` the default stage does not refuse yet: an integer wider than
-- its field, a growable array default, and an unknown constructor default. It warns and
-- truncates `300` into a `U8`, and refuses the other two only as unbuilt ("does not implement
-- this constant expression yet"). Move each back when it does.

data Direction = North | South

data TooBig {value: U8 = 300}

-- A growable array allocates its run, so there is nothing constant about one: the storage would
-- have to exist before the program starts. `[T *n]` is the shape that does have a constant form,
-- since its elements are the value's own bytes.
data Grown {items: Array(Int) = [1, 2]}

-- A name that is no constructor at all.
data Unknown {heading: Direction = West}

fn main() -> Int = 0
